  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "Counted unit: the article's Theorem (source0.tex lines 2677--2698, source label thm:olg_well_posed): for any continuous interest-rate profile there exists a lifespan bound depending on the data for which the overlapping generations model under incomplete markets admits a general equilibrium interest rate, and for any capital profile and radius there is a further lifespan bound for which the equilibrium rate lies within that radius plus a norm term; delivered with the article's complete original proof at source0.tex lines 2700--2863 (one adjacent proof environment of 164 lines that opens and closes inside the retained span). The proof is complete and closed inside the retained span together with its retained context: it reformulates the equilibrium condition as a fixed-point problem for the map sending an interest-rate profile to the equilibrium rate of the life-cycle problem, uses the retained regularity and stability results to show that this map sends a closed bounded set of continuous profiles into itself, proves that it is a contraction on that set by combining the retained growth-stability and two-parameter integral estimates, and concludes existence and the stated bound through the contraction principle. This theorem is the well-posedness result that underpins the article's stochastic analysis of overlapping generations models under incomplete markets. H2: a research-level mathematical-economics theorem whose proof combines the life-cycle problem, demographic-flow estimates, a fixed-point reformulation and a quantitative contraction argument built from the article's stability lemmas; it is well beyond ordinary PhD qualifying exercises.",
